Amazon Web Services:-
Services offered by amazon using cloud that can be accessed virtually.
-Root user
  One who access to all the services on the console.
-IAM user(Identity Access Management)
  Creating users that can access the granted sevices by the root user on the console
  -User:Gets the authentication to access the console with authorized services.
  -User Groups:The users who are involved in same serives come in same group.
  -Policies:The only granted services can be used other services are highly secured.
  -Roles:For accessing one cloud from another cloud.


-EC2(Elastic cloud computing)
  For creating virtual servers that are elastic,elastic here means can be managed even after creating.
  1.General
  2.Compute optimized
  3.Memory
  4.Storage
  5.Accelerated
  The data center for ec2 instances can also be modified according to user requirements,we can choose nearest available aws data centers.
  Each region has multiple availability zones in case the main one goes down so it switches to the other availability zone. 
